WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:02.837
A replay can finish and still say Not
ready.

00:00:03.007 --> 00:00:07.210
The readiness scorecard tells you which
checks are holding back the build and gives

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.273
you a place to start.

00:00:08.819 --> 00:00:12.980
Open a completed Speedscale replay report
and select Readiness.

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:15.244
Start with What gets this build to ready.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:19.693
Here, both Regression and Resilience are
below their required grades.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:23.354
The tiles under Must pass to ship can block
the verdict.

00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:25.709
Regression is a D and needs a B.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.204
The advisory tiles can still guide your
investigation.

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:31.572
This time, open Regression first.

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:35.110
The family detail shows how the grade was
computed.

00:00:35.281 --> 00:00:40.152
Here, ninety-two point six percent of
assertions passed, and the B floor requires

00:00:40.152 --> 00:00:41.415
ninety-eight percent.

00:00:41.585 --> 00:00:43.785
The scorecard shows what needs to improve.

00:00:44.352 --> 00:00:45.647
Scroll to Findings.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:50.542
The first row shows status-code assertion
failures for the account lookup endpoint.

00:00:50.713 --> 00:00:54.603
The count tells you how many times that
finding occurred in this replay.

00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:59.193
Click Open Requests to inspect the
transactions behind the family.

00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:02.855
Compare recorded and replayed responses to
see what changed.

00:01:03.026 --> 00:01:07.898
Fix the problem, rerun the replay, and
return to Readiness to check both blockers.

00:01:08.452 --> 00:01:10.752
Use the Readiness verdict on the new report

00:01:10.752 --> 00:01:13.641
to see whether the build meets your
configured floors.
